 The list of discovered PuppetDB targets is refreshed at the interval, which can be configured via `-promscrape.puppetdbSDCheckInterval` command-line flag.
 
+## scaleway_sd_configs
+
+Scaleway SD configuration allows retrieving scrape targets from [Scaleway](https://www.scaleway.com/) Instances API.
+
+Configuration example:
+
+```yaml
+scrape_configs:
+- job_name: scaleway
+  scaleway_sd_configs:
+
+    # server is an optional Scaleway API server to query.
+    # By default, https://api.scaleway.com is used.
+    #
+  - server: "https://api.scaleway.com"
+
+    # zone is the Scaleway zone to discover Instances in, e.g. "fr-par-1".
+    # By default, "fr-par-1" is used.
+    #
+    # zone: <string> | default = "fr-par-1"
+
+    # project is an optional Scaleway project ID to filter discovered Instances by.
+    #
+    # project: <string>
+
+    # port is the port to scrape metrics from.
+    #
+    # port: <int> | default = 80
+
+    # Scaleway's Instances API authenticates via a plain `X-Auth-Token` header rather than
+    # an OAuth2/Bearer scheme, so the API secret key is passed via the generic `headers` option:
+    #
+    headers:
+    - "X-Auth-Token: <secret_key>"
+
+    # Additional HTTP API client options can be specified here, e.g. proxy_url.
+    # See https://docs.victoriametrics.com/victoriametrics/sd_configs/#http-api-client-options
+```
+
+Only Instances in the `running` state are discovered. Discovered targets' address defaults
+to `<public_ip>:<port>`, where `<public_ip>` is the public IPv4 address of the Instance and `<port>`
+is the port specified in the `scaleway_sd_configs`. If the Instance has no public IPv4 address, its
+private IPv4 address is used instead.
+
+The following meta labels are available on discovered targets during relabeling:
+
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_id`: the ID of the Instance.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_name`: the name of the Instance.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_status`: the state of the Instance (always `running`, since only running Instances are discovered).
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_type`: the commercial type of the Instance.
+* `__meta_scaleway_zone`: the zone of the Instance.
+* `__meta_scaleway_project_id`: the ID of the project the Instance belongs to.
+* `__meta_scaleway_public_ipv4`: the public IPv4 of the Instance.
+* `__meta_scaleway_private_ipv4`: the private IPv4 of the Instance.
+* `__meta_scaleway_tags`: the comma-separated list of tags of the Instance.
+
+The list of discovered Scaleway targets is refreshed at the interval, which can be configured via `-promscrape.scalewaySDCheckInterval` command-line flag.
+
 ## static_configs
 
 A static config allows specifying a list of targets and a common label set for them.
